      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes and no.\nLast events can\u0027t save us from b/301141955.\nAnd probably mPollEventCounts is not enough too.\nBut they are good in general issue clarification I think.\n\nFor b/301141955, in a subsequent CL, the plan is to add uid, and callstack for system uids.\nSo we can do something like:\nforceUpdate() {\n  final PollEvent event;\n  if (uid \u003d\u003d SYSTEM_UID) {\n    event \u003d new PollEvent(POLL_REASON_FORCE_UPDATE, uid, getCallStack());\n  } else {\n    event \u003d new PollEvent(POLL_REASON_FORCE_UPDATE, uid);\n  }\n  performPoll(flag, event);\n}  \n\nThus, in NetworkStatsEventLogger, we can check if these fields are filled and\nstore such info into something like:\n\n  // String[] is the file name list strip from getCallStrackTrace()\n  HashMap\u003cString[], Int\u003e mCountPerSystemCallers;\n  \n  logPollEvent(...) {\n     ...\n     if (event.uid \u003d\u003d SYSTEM_UID \u0026\u0026 event.callstack !\u003d null) {\n       mCountPerSystemCallers.put(event.callstack, /* previous count +1 */);\n     }\n  } \n  \nIf so, we can dump poll counts per system caller like:\n\n  dump(..) {\n       ....\n       pw.println(\"Poll counts per system caller:\");\n       ...\n  }\n  \nI think this might be a way out for b/301141955.\nWDYT?",
